 // A sweep alone halts dead on contact, which is right for "stop at the
 // surface" and wrong for everything after it: pushing the pointer into the
 // floor while moving sideways stopped the piece entirely, so dragging ALONG
 // a surface meant lifting and re-dragging, over and over. The retry keeps
 // whichever component of the motion the obstacle doesn't oppose — X first,
 // then Y from where X ended — which is exactly "slide along the floor".
